            <div xml:id="d625">

                <pb facs="0623" n="611" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg611"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.94/55: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-02T22:00:00+09:00">November 2, 1937—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 2—10:28 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>514. 1. The evening papers report that the Cabinet today approved an important
                    diplomatic document which was then submitted to the Emperor for approval; that
                    after examination by the Privy Council and approval by the Emperor the document
                    will be signed.</p>
                <p>2. The document under reference is believed to be a treaty with Italy to combat
                    communism probably with an additional secret clause.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
